 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 12995,
   "ANSWER": "<ul data-end=\"1701\" data-start=\"932\">\n\t<li data-end=\"982\" data-start=\"932\">\n\t<p data-end=\"982\" data-start=\"934\">New jobs enter the highest-priority queue (Q0)</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1032\" data-start=\"983\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1032\" data-start=\"985\">If not completed in 8 ms, moved to Q1 (16 ms)</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1161\" data-start=\"1033\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1161\" data-start=\"1035\">If still not completed, moved to Q2 (FCFS) <strong>(30%)</strong><br />\n\t| <strong data-end=\"1116\" data-start=\"1096\">Process Movement</strong> | - Processes demoted on excessive CPU use</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1214\" data-start=\"1162\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1214\" data-start=\"1164\">Processes promoted (aging) to prevent starvation</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1266\" data-start=\"1215\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1266\" data-start=\"1217\">Example: A CPU-bound process moves Q0 &rarr; Q1 &rarr; Q2</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1414\" data-start=\"1267\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1414\" data-start=\"1269\">An I/O-bound or interactive process may remain in Q0 <strong>(30%)</strong><br />\n\t| <strong data-end=\"1360\" data-start=\"1340\">Example Scenario</strong> | - Describe a sample process P1 using 25 ms of CPU</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1473\" data-start=\"1415\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1473\" data-start=\"1417\">P1 starts in Q0 (uses 8 ms) &rarr; moves to Q1 (uses 16 ms)</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1619\" data-start=\"1474\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1619\" data-start=\"1476\">Remaining 1 ms served in Q2 (FCFS) <strong>(20%)</strong><br />\n\t| <strong data-end=\"1554\" data-start=\"1529\">Starvation Prevention</strong> | - Aging used to move long-waiting processes to higher queues</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1701\" data-start=\"1620\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1701\" data-start=\"1622\">Prevents low-priority processes from being indefinitely delayed <strong>(20%)</strong></p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
