   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p data-end=\"450\" data-start=\"338\"><strong data-end=\"447\" data-start=\"347\">Explain the working of a Multilevel Feedback Queue (MLFQ) with an example involving three queues</strong>:</p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"550\" data-start=\"451\">\n\t<li data-end=\"493\" data-start=\"451\">\n\t<p data-end=\"493\" data-start=\"453\">Q0: Round Robin with time quantum 8 ms</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"537\" data-start=\"494\">\n\t<p data-end=\"537\" data-start=\"496\">Q1: Round Robin with time quantum 16 ms</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"550\" data-start=\"538\">\n\t<p data-end=\"550\" data-start=\"540\">Q2: FCFS</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p data-end=\"635\" data-start=\"552\">Illustrate how a process moves between queues and how the system avoids starvation.</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 309,
